Never mind, and pardon me--my mistake. The structural model is a simplex, with paths
f1 0.5 f2
f2 0.5 f3
but with no direct path between f1 and f3. So f3 and f1 have correlation 0.25, not 0.5. The correlations between f1 and f2 and between f2 and f3 are 0.5. THAT is why there is a tiny difference in the z statistics for the residual variances.
--Ed Rigdon

